  <h1 style="font-size: 16px; font-weight: bold; margin: 0;">GENERAL CONDITIONS OF CONTRACT</h1>
  <p style="font-size: 10px; margin: 6px 0 0 0;">For Detached Dwellings and Associated Work</p>
</div>

<p style="font-size: 9px; text-align: center; margin-bottom: 16px; color: #666;">
  These General Conditions form part of the QBCC Building Contract and are regulated by the
  <em>Queensland Building and Construction Commission Act 1991</em> and the
  <em>Domestic Building Contracts Act 2000</em>.
</p>

<h2 style="font-size: 12px; background: #000; color: #fff; padding: 4px 8px; margin: 12px 0 6px 0;">1. INTERPRETATION</h2>

<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 6px 0;"><strong>1.1</strong> In this contract, unless the context otherwise requires:</p>
<ul style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 6px 12px; padding: 0;">
  <li><strong>"Building Work"</strong> means the work described in the contract</li>
  <li><strong>"Contract Price"</strong> means the total price stated in the contract (including GST)</li>
  <li><strong>"Contractor"</strong> means the licensed builder named in the contract</li>
  <li><strong>"Defect"</strong> means any failure to meet the requirements of the contract or applicable standards</li>
  <li><strong>"Owner"</strong> means the person(s) named as owner in the contract</li>
  <li><strong>"Practical Completion"</strong> means when the building work is complete except for minor omissions and defects</li>
  <li><strong>"Site"</strong> means the land where the building work is to be carried out</li>
  <li><strong>"Working Day"</strong> means a day other than a Saturday, Sunday, public holiday, or builder's holiday period</li>
</ul>

<h2 style="font-size: 12px; background: #000; color: #fff; padding: 4px 8px; margin: 12px 0 6px 0;">2. CONTRACTOR'S OBLIGATIONS</h2>

<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 4px 0;"><strong>2.1</strong> The contractor must:</p>
<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 2px 12px;">(a) carry out the building work in accordance with the contract, plans, and specifications;</p>
<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 2px 12px;">(b) comply with all applicable laws, codes, and standards;</p>
<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 2px 12px;">(c) use materials that are new (unless otherwise specified) and fit for purpose;</p>
<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 2px 12px;">(d) carry out the work in a proper and workmanlike manner;</p>
<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 2px 12px;">(e) obtain all necessary approvals and permits;</p>
<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 6px 12px;">(f) maintain public liability and workers' compensation insurance.</p>

<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 6px 0;"><strong>2.2</strong> The contractor must give the owner reasonable notice before commencing any stage of the work.</p>

<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 6px 0;"><strong>2.3</strong> The contractor must maintain the site in a reasonably clean and safe condition.</p>

<h2 style="font-size: 12px; background: #000; color: #fff; padding: 4px 8px; margin: 12px 0 6px 0;">3. OWNER'S OBLIGATIONS</h2>

<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 4px 0;"><strong>3.1</strong> The owner must:</p>
<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 2px 12px;">(a) give the contractor uninterrupted access to the site;</p>
<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 2px 12px;">(b) pay the contract price and any approved variations as required;</p>
<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 2px 12px;">(c) make selections (colours, fittings) within the required timeframes;</p>
<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 6px 12px;">(d) not interfere with the building work or give directions to subcontractors.</p>

<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 6px 0;"><strong>3.2</strong> The owner must ensure the site is free from hazards and disclose any known conditions that may affect the work.</p>

<h2 style="font-size: 12px; background: #000; color: #fff; padding: 4px 8px; margin: 12px 0 6px 0;">4. PROGRESS PAYMENTS</h2>

<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 6px 0;"><strong>4.1</strong> The contractor may only claim progress payments when a stage specified in the contract is complete.</p>

<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 6px 0;"><strong>4.2</strong> A progress claim must be in writing and include:</p>
<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 2px 12px;">(a) the stage of work completed;</p>
<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 2px 12px;">(b) the amount claimed; and</p>
<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 6px 12px;">(c) any amounts for variations approved in writing.</p>

<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 6px 0;"><strong>4.3</strong> The owner must pay progress claims within 5 business days of receiving the claim, unless the owner disputes the claim in writing within that period.</p>

<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 6px 0;"><strong>4.4</strong> If payment is not made when due, the contractor may:</p>
<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 2px 12px;">(a) charge interest at the rate specified in the Penalty Interest Rates Act 1962;</p>
<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 6px 12px;">(b) suspend work (after giving 5 business days' written notice).</p>

<h2 style="font-size: 12px; background: #000; color: #fff; padding: 4px 8px; margin: 12px 0 6px 0;">5. VARIATIONS</h2>

<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 6px 0;"><strong>5.1</strong> No variation to the contract is binding unless agreed in writing by both parties before the varied work commences.</p>

<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 6px 0;"><strong>5.2</strong> A written variation must specify:</p>
<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 2px 12px;">(a) the nature of the varied work;</p>
<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 2px 12px;">(b) the cost (addition or deduction); and</p>
<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 6px 12px;">(c) any adjustment to the building period.</p>

<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 6px 0;"><strong>5.3</strong> If the owner requests a variation, the contractor must provide a written quote within a reasonable time.</p>

<h2 style="font-size: 12px; background: #000; color: #fff; padding: 4px 8px; margin: 12px 0 6px 0;">6. BUILDING PERIOD AND EXTENSIONS</h2>

<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 6px 0;"><strong>6.1</strong> The contractor must complete the building work within the building period stated in the contract.</p>

<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 6px 0;"><strong>6.2</strong> The building period is extended by any delay caused by:</p>
<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 2px 12px;">(a) inclement weather (rain, excessive heat, high winds);</p>
<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 2px 12px;">(b) approved variations;</p>
<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 2px 12px;">(c) late selections by the owner;</p>
<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 2px 12px;">(d) delays in obtaining approvals (not caused by the contractor);</p>
<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 2px 12px;">(e) industrial disputes;</p>
<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 2px 12px;">(f) material or labour shortages beyond the contractor's control;</p>
<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 6px 12px;">(g) any other cause beyond the contractor's reasonable control.</p>

<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 6px 0;"><strong>6.3</strong> The contractor must notify the owner in writing of any delay and the expected extension.</p>

<h2 style="font-size: 12px; background: #000; color: #fff; padding: 4px 8px; margin: 12px 0 6px 0;">7. PRACTICAL COMPLETION</h2>

<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 6px 0;"><strong>7.1</strong> When the contractor believes practical completion has been reached, the contractor must notify the owner in writing.</p>

<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 6px 0;"><strong>7.2</strong> Within 5 business days of notification, the owner and contractor must inspect the building together.</p>

<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 6px 0;"><strong>7.3</strong> Following the inspection, the contractor must provide a list of any minor defects or omissions and the date by which they will be completed (being not more than 7 days after practical completion).</p>

<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 6px 0;"><strong>7.4</strong> The final payment is due upon practical completion, subject to retention for any incomplete items.</p>

<h2 style="font-size: 12px; background: #000; color: #fff; padding: 4px 8px; margin: 12px 0 6px 0;">8. DEFECTS LIABILITY</h2>

<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 6px 0;"><strong>8.1</strong> The contractor must rectify any defects notified by the owner:</p>
<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 2px 12px;">(a) within 6 months of practical completion for non-structural defects;</p>
<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 6px 12px;">(b) within 6 years and 6 months for structural defects, subsidence, or settlement.</p>

<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 6px 0;"><strong>8.2</strong> The contractor is not liable for defects caused by:</p>
<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 2px 12px;">(a) normal wear and tear;</p>
<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 2px 12px;">(b) misuse or failure to maintain by the owner;</p>
<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 6px 12px;">(c) work or materials supplied by the owner.</p>

<h2 style="font-size: 12px; background: #000; color: #fff; padding: 4px 8px; margin: 12px 0 6px 0;">9. INSURANCE</h2>

<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 6px 0;"><strong>9.1</strong> The contractor must maintain:</p>
<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 2px 12px;">(a) public liability insurance of not less than $5,000,000;</p>
<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 6px 12px;">(b) workers' compensation insurance as required by law.</p>

<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 6px 0;"><strong>9.2</strong> QBCC home warranty insurance automatically applies to contracts over $3,300.</p>

<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 6px 0;"><strong>9.3</strong> The owner is responsible for insuring the building work from practical completion.</p>

<h2 style="font-size: 12px; background: #000; color: #fff; padding: 4px 8px; margin: 12px 0 6px 0;">10. TERMINATION</h2>

<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 6px 0;"><strong>10.1</strong> Either party may terminate this contract if the other party:</p>
<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 2px 12px;">(a) is in substantial breach of the contract; and</p>
<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 6px 12px;">(b) fails to remedy that breach within 10 business days of written notice.</p>

<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 6px 0;"><strong>10.2</strong> If the contract is terminated:</p>
<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 2px 12px;">(a) the contractor is entitled to payment for work completed;</p>
<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 6px 12px;">(b) the non-defaulting party may claim damages for breach.</p>

<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 6px 0;"><strong>10.3</strong> If the contractor becomes insolvent or has their QBCC licence suspended, the owner may terminate immediately.</p>

<h2 style="font-size: 12px; background: #000; color: #fff; padding: 4px 8px; margin: 12px 0 6px 0;">11. DISPUTE RESOLUTION</h2>

<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 6px 0;"><strong>11.1</strong> If a dispute arises, the parties must first attempt to resolve it by:</p>
<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 2px 12px;">(a) written notice specifying the dispute;</p>
<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 6px 12px;">(b) meeting within 10 business days to negotiate a resolution.</p>

<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 6px 0;"><strong>11.2</strong> If the dispute cannot be resolved, either party may:</p>
<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 2px 12px;">(a) lodge a complaint with the QBCC; or</p>
<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 6px 12px;">(b) pursue remedies through QCAT or the courts.</p>

<h2 style="font-size: 12px; background: #000; color: #fff; padding: 4px 8px; margin: 12px 0 6px 0;">12. GENERAL PROVISIONS</h2>

<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 6px 0;"><strong>12.1</strong> Notices under this contract must be in writing and may be delivered by hand, post, or email to the address in the contract.</p>

<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 6px 0;"><strong>12.2</strong> This contract is governed by the laws of Queensland.</p>

<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 6px 0;"><strong>12.3</strong> Nothing in this contract limits or excludes any statutory warranties or consumer guarantees under law.</p>

<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 6px 0;"><strong>12.4</strong> If any provision of this contract is invalid or unenforceable, the remaining provisions remain in force.</p>

<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 6px 0;"><strong>12.5</strong> This contract constitutes the entire agreement between the parties and supersedes all prior negotiations and representations.</p>

<h2 style="font-size: 12px; background: #000; color: #fff; padding: 4px 8px; margin: 16px 0 6px 0;">ACKNOWLEDGEMENT</h2>

<p style="font-size: 9px; margin: 0 0 16px 0;">
  I/We acknowledge that I/we have received, read, and understood these General Conditions of Contract
  which form part of the building contract.
</p>

